## Ethical Position

FTP2.0 explores how AI-generated interpretations can influence the way people understand themselves and their interactions.

The project foregrounds participant agency: an interpretation should invite reflection, not claim unquestionable authority. Its design principles include meaningful consent, separation between live interaction and post-session interpretation, transparency, and scrutiny of data flows.

These principles are design intentions, not a claim of independent privacy or security certification.

## The Central Question

> When AI systems participate in how we communicate and interpret ourselves, who gets to define the meaning?

**Interpretation is not ownership.**

